Dr. Quark burst into The Johnny's office at precisely 7:47 AM, clutching a tablet to his chest like a sacred text. "The phase variance compensator worked. We've confirmed it\'97different gravitational constants in at least seventeen parallel universes."\
The Johnny looked up from his morning routine of admiring his reflection in his phone's camera. "Different universes? Prove it."\
Quark's fingers danced across the tablet, projecting a holographic display. Mathematical equations floated in the air like fireflies. "Each message carries a gravitational signature. The variance is minute\'97parts per billion\'97but consistent. Here..." He highlighted one section. "This universe has gravity 0.00023% stronger than ours. Time must pass more quickly there."\
"Fascinating." The Johnny stood, already calculating how this discovery would sound in his progress report to Sarah. "And you're certain these are actual messages, not random noise?"\
"The patterns are too regular. And look at this." Quark expanded another equation. "When I aligned the phase compensators to match a universe's gravitational constant, the message clarity increased by 300%. These aren't random signals\'97they're deliberate communication."\
The office door chimed. Chip Stockwell entered, looking uncomfortable in his crisp new Shakti Enterprises lab coat. "Mr. Stoat? Eloise Shakti said I should report here for Project Kebab."\
"Ah, the Fridge Force defector." The Johnny sized up Chip with the practiced disdain of someone who needed to establish dominance immediately. "Tell me, Stockwell, what do you know about quantum entanglement across dimensional barriers?"\
Chip blinked. "That's... not within my expertise. But stasis technology does involve temporal field manipulation, and there are strict protocols about preventing resonance between\'97"\
"Fascinating." The Johnny cut him off. "Quark, brief our new hire on the gravitational variance findings. I need to prepare for the morning briefing."\
As Quark began explaining his discoveries, Chip's expression grew increasingly concerned. "Dr. Quark, if you're detecting messages from universes with different gravitational constants, have you considered the temporal displacement factor? If two universes are exchanging signals and one has time flowing faster\'97"\
"We haven't tested any active communication yet," Quark reassured him.\
"Good. In Fridge Force training, we learned that temporal synchronization across dimensional barriers is theoretically impossible. Any attempt creates\'97"\
"Creates what?" The Johnny interrupted, suddenly interested.\
Chip hesitated. "The exact details are classified, but let's just say there's a reason we maintain strict isolation protocols for all stasis fields."\
The office door opened again, and Chilo Windus glided in. "Good morning, gentlemen. I couldn't help overhearing your discussion. Temporal displacement across parallel dimensions? How intriguing."\
"We're discovering that messages from different universes carry unique gravitational signatures," Quark explained eagerly.\
Chilo nodded thoughtfully. "Have you considered that these universes might exist in different temporal states? What you perceive as a message from the past could be simultaneous communication from a universe where time flows differently."\
"That's exactly what concerns me," Chip interjected. "If we attempt any form of active response without proper temporal calibration\'97"\
"Then we might accidentally alter both timelines," Chilo finished, but his tone suggested excitement rather than warning. "Though perhaps that's the point. Perhaps these other civilizations are reaching out specifically because they need our help to synchronize temporal flows."\
The Johnny's eyes lit up with the gleam of someone who'd just spotted a shortcut to glory. "That's brilliant. Quark, add temporal calculations to your variance compensator. We need to be ready for two-way communication."\
"Sir, I really must protest\'97" Chip began.\
"Your protest is noted and dismissed, Stockwell. If you're too timid for groundbreaking research, perhaps Eloise made a mistake bringing you here."\
Chip's jaw clenched, but he said nothing. As the others continued discussing modifications to the equipment, he quietly excused himself, already composing a warning in his head for Dr. Logan.\
Chilo watched him go with a slight smile. Soon, the tour would begin, and the real experiments could commence.\
